./docs/IPFS_DATASETS_PY_DEPENDENCY_MAP.md:7:This document turns the `ipfs_datasets_py` integration roadmap into an explicit dependency map.
./docs/IPFS_DATASETS_PY_DEPENDENCY_MAP.md:17:1. how runtime information should flow through complaint-generator
./docs/IPFS_DATASETS_PY_DEPENDENCY_MAP.md:20:This map should be read against the current repo state, not an earlier greenfield baseline. Complaint-generator already has persisted evidence and authority facts, queue-backed scraper execution, graph-support fallback summaries, and review payloads that expose coverage plus lineage-aware follow-up plan, execution, and history summaries. The dependency question is therefore how to deepen those existing slices into a complete graph, retrieval, and reasoning system.
./docs/IPFS_DATASETS_PY_DEPENDENCY_MAP.md:85:- `mediator/mediator.py` remains the orchestrator.
./docs/IPFS_DATASETS_PY_DEPENDENCY_MAP.md:86:- `complaint_phases/` remains the canonical in-memory graph workflow.
./docs/IPFS_DATASETS_PY_DEPENDENCY_MAP.md:89:- the shared case outputs that matter most are the existing fact registry, claim-support store, future persisted coverage matrix, and review packets.
./docs/IPFS_DATASETS_PY_DEPENDENCY_MAP.md:95:| Orchestration | `mediator/mediator.py` | phase progression, follow-up planning, review payloads |
./docs/IPFS_DATASETS_PY_DEPENDENCY_MAP.md:96:| Storage and provenance | `mediator/evidence_hooks.py`, `integrations/ipfs_datasets/storage.py` | reproducible artifact storage and source lineage |
./docs/IPFS_DATASETS_PY_DEPENDENCY_MAP.md:97:| Web acquisition | `mediator/web_evidence_hooks.py`, `integrations/ipfs_datasets/search.py` | search, fetch, archive, temporal metadata |
./docs/IPFS_DATASETS_PY_DEPENDENCY_MAP.md:98:| Legal acquisition | `mediator/legal_authority_hooks.py`, `integrations/ipfs_datasets/legal.py` | authority retrieval, normalization, ranking |
./docs/IPFS_DATASETS_PY_DEPENDENCY_MAP.md:99:| Parsing | `integrations/ipfs_datasets/documents.py` plus mediator ingestion hooks | text extraction, chunking, metadata, OCR fallback |
./docs/IPFS_DATASETS_PY_DEPENDENCY_MAP.md:100:| Facts and support | `mediator/claim_support_hooks.py` plus the current fact registry substrate | claim-element support organization |
./docs/IPFS_DATASETS_PY_DEPENDENCY_MAP.md:101:| Graph enrichment | `integrations/ipfs_datasets/graphs.py`, `complaint_phases/` | support edges, entity resolution, graph persistence |
./docs/IPFS_DATASETS_PY_DEPENDENCY_MAP.md:104:| Queue-backed acquisition | `mediator/evidence_hooks.py`, `mediator/mediator.py`, `scripts/agentic_scraper_cli.py` | deferred worker execution and queue inspection |
./docs/IPFS_DATASETS_PY_DEPENDENCY_MAP.md:105:| Review outputs | mediator reporting layer | support packet, contradiction report, provenance bundle |
./docs/IPFS_DATASETS_PY_DEPENDENCY_MAP.md:141:The scraper worker should consume queued work rather than running indefinitely without demand. This keeps archival and evidence acquisition aligned with real follow-up tasks and avoids idle scraping that produces unreviewed noise.
./docs/IPFS_DATASETS_PY_DEPENDENCY_MAP.md:149:### 4. Graph queries before review surfaces
