./docs/PAYLOAD_CONTRACTS.md:3103:- Resolution events are append-only ledger rows under `claim_follow_up_execution`; they do not overwrite the original `skipped_manual_review` event.
./docs/PAYLOAD_CONTRACTS.md:3104:- `related_execution_id` should point at the original manual-review audit row when available, so the resolution can be traced back to the triggering contradiction workflow.
./docs/PAYLOAD_CONTRACTS.md:3105:- `resolution_metadata` is merged into the stored ledger metadata and is intended for reviewer identity, rationale, or downstream workflow tags.
./docs/PAYLOAD_CONTRACTS.md:3106:- `post_resolution_review` reuses the same review contract as `POST /api/claim-support/review`, making the updated history and summary immediately available after resolution.
