./docs/PAYLOAD_CONTRACTS.md:3284:- `graph_gap_query` is the compact routing packet derived from `graph_gap_context` plus the claim element and missing support kinds. It is suitable for queue workers and dashboards that need to distinguish graph-backed support review from empty retrieval lanes without reading `graph_support.results`.
./docs/PAYLOAD_CONTRACTS.md:3285:- `recommended_action` distinguishes ordinary retrieval from more specific modes such as `collect_fact_support` when rule candidates already identify the missing factual predicate, or `review_adverse_authority` when current authority support is adverse.
./docs/PAYLOAD_CONTRACTS.md:3293:- `authority_treatment_summary` carries the same supportive versus adverse authority signal used by claim coverage and review payloads, so planner consumers can tell when a task is driven by questioned or limiting authority rather than missing citations alone.
./docs/PAYLOAD_CONTRACTS.md:3294:- `temporal_rule_profile_id`, `temporal_rule_status`, `temporal_rule_blocking_reasons`, and `temporal_rule_follow_ups` surface the exact chronology rule failure and the recommended repair prompt so review clients, exports, and CLI summaries can explain why the task exists.
